$NetBSD$

Three things in the src makefile.

Put @LIBXPM@ on the Xaw link line.  Xaw itself is sometimes linked against Xpm,
and then -lXaw alone leaves Xpm symbols unresolved.  patch-configure.in adds
the test that fills this in:

	AC_CHECK_LIB(Xaw, XawPixmapsInitialize, [ LIBXPM="-lXpm" ], [ LIBXPM=""])

LINKER is $(CC) -nostdlib, which drops the standard libraries as well as the
startup files.  -nostartfiles is what was meant.

Drop the "bytecomp" target.  It comes from the Mule 4.1b patch, not from
emacs, and it runs the dumped emacs to byte-compile five lisp files -- but
dumping needs those .elc files to exist first, so it runs a step too late to
be of use.  The five are fetched instead, as emacs-20.7-mule-4.1b-elc.tar.gz;
its README says why:

	These files have to be ditributed separately since in Emacs build
	Emacs needs *.elc files to dump from temacs; on the other hand,
	Emacs can't (or very difficult) do byte compile Emacs lisp files
	before dumped.

		Masao Uebayashi <uebayasi@netbsd.org>

The paxctl calls that used to be in here are patch-pax-aslr now; they are a
different kind of change and the other emacs packages need the same one.

--- src/Makefile.in.orig	2016-11-26 06:25:26.875919180 +0000
+++ src/Makefile.in
@@ -329,7 +329,7 @@ LIBXMENU=
 #ifdef USE_X_TOOLKIT
 #define @X_TOOLKIT_TYPE@
 #if defined (LUCID) || defined (ATHENA)
-LIBW= -lXaw
+LIBW= -lXaw @LIBXPM@
 #endif
 #ifdef MOTIF
 #if defined (HAVE_MOTIF_2_1) && defined (HAVE_LIBXP)
@@ -402,7 +402,7 @@ LIBX= $(LIBXMENU) LD_SWITCH_X_SITE -lX10
    ask GCC explicitly where to find libgcc.a.  */
 
 #ifndef LINKER
-#define LINKER $(CC) -nostdlib
+#define LINKER $(CC) -nostartfiles
 #endif
 
 #ifndef LIB_GCC
@@ -804,14 +804,7 @@ LIBES = $(LOADLIBES) $(LDLIBS) $(LIBX) L
 #define OBJECTS_MACHINE
 #endif
 
-all: emacs bytecomp OTHER_FILES
-
-bytecomp: emacs
-	./emacs -batch -q -f batch-byte-compile \
-	${lispsource}ange-ftp.el ${lispsource}international/ccl.el \
-	${lispsource}international/mule-cmds.el \
-	${lispsource}international/mule.el \
-	${lispsource}international/titdic-cnv.el
+all: emacs OTHER_FILES
 
 emacs: temacs ${etc}DOC ${lisp}
 #ifdef CANNOT_DUMP
